    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span><span class=\"time\">15 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip ok\">Easy</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Two pointers</span><span class=\"chip accent\">In-place compaction</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/remove-duplicates-from-sorted-array/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 26</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Remove Duplicates from Sorted Array</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Sorted input puts equal values side by side, so a value is new exactly when it differs from the last value you kept. A read pointer scans, a write pointer stores each new value: one pass, O(n) time, O(1) space.</p>\n"
